WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:04.420
While it might've seemed like the Saw series
was "game over" when the seventh installment

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.540
came out in 2010, there was still a lot of
bloodshed to be had on the big screen.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:13.540
With a little revisionist history, some new
and confusing characters, and even more disgusting

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:17.810
traps to behold, the eighth installment to
the Saw franchise has an even more complex

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.500
relationship to the original story than the
other sequels.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.680
So, let's walk through how exactly Jigsaw
fits into the overall puzzle, shall we?

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.100
Face the spoilers or click away now…

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.380
"Make your choice."

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.240
Still dead

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.740
One of the biggest questions facing the Saw
revival was how the filmmakers would deal

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:39.540
with the demise of the franchise's primary
antagonist, John Kramer, a.k.a. Jigsaw.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:44.600
Unlike Jason Voorhees or Michael Myers, Jigsaw
never had any supernatural powers; he was

00:00:44.609 --> 00:00:48.909
just a wickedly brilliant guy with an axe
to grind—and, eventually, a terminal case

00:00:48.909 --> 00:00:49.540
of cancer.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.800
So imagine the audience's surprise when John
Kramer shows up to stage a new grisly test

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:54.900
series in Jigsaw.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.209
Yes, it's the same guy who was laid out cold
and in the buff on the autopsy table in Saw

00:00:59.209 --> 00:01:03.819
IV, and he's definitely alive when we see
him in this movie … but he hasn't magically

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:04.740
risen from the grave.

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:09.540
Instead, his newest group trap series actually
takes place 10 years in the past, even though

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.720
some clever editing that suggests otherwise.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:16.600
And while it looks like there are five victims
to bite the dust, there is one guy who secretly

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.960
walks away from the whole thing.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:19.700
Settling the score

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:24.360
In the beginning of Jigsaw's group trap, there's
one man who's left behind during the first

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.409
test because he's not even awake for it.

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:28.560
But it turns out, that guy doesn't bite it
after all.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:32.960
Logan Nelson, who's been analyzing all the
new bodies popping up with Jigsaw puzzle pieces

00:01:32.969 --> 00:01:37.060
carved out of them, seems like a nice guy
throughout the movie … until we learn that

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.500
he's actually Jigsaw's secret protege.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:45.100
As it turns out, early in his career, he mis-labeled
John's brain scans, which may have made difference

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.540
in his treatment and prognosis.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:50.680
But even though Jigsaw's willing to put him
into the group game for his mistake, he changes

00:01:50.689 --> 00:01:54.689
his mind and decides he doesn't want Logan
to bleed out over a simple workplace error

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:56.540
and decides to train him instead.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:00.240
Whether he's ever worked with any of the other
Jigsaw minions remains to be seen.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.000
A game of his own

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:07.020
The new bodies that are popping up around
town belong to victims of Logan's modern copycat

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:11.080
game, and have each escaped real punishment
for their various crimes, thanks to Detective

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.740
Halloren's questionable ethics.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:16.560
One of these people is Edgar Munsen, who's
shot by police after claiming to hold the

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.230
lives of five others in his hands with a remote
control.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.260
He just so happens to have been the man who
attacked Logan's wife, but was let off easy

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:23.980
by Halloren.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.780
But it's not just his wife's fate that makes
Logan hate Halloren.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.080
He also had a girl about his daughter's age
pop up on his autopsy table who was attacked

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:35.580
by a guy who bribed Halloren, so he wants
to stop the bad cop in the worst way possible.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:39.360
And all of the people who've perished in this
new round of games are dangerous perps who

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.450
Halloren has let off the hook recently.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:42.900
Eye on the prize

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.670
As the body count climbs, Halloren starts
to suspect Logan's Jigsaw-obsessed assistant

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.080
Eleanor, and for good reason.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:53.700
She's been re-creating Jigsaw's most infamous
traps from dark-web-scoured blueprints and

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.880
seems oddly fascinated by his history.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:00.480
Once Logan's old combat buddy Detective Hunt
catches wind of her sinister little studio,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.460
he starts to buy into the theory that Logan
and Eleanor are behind these fresh homicides.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:09.330
However, Logan plants some key evidence that
points at Halloren being responsible for everything

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:12.000
and sets up for a final grudge match with
Halloren himself.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:13.720
A big showdown

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:17.880
There are only three bodies that emerge from
Logan's games, which is two fewer than the

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.880
casualties of Jigsaw's original scene.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.840
Jigsaw's final two victims' bodies have never
been discovered and are still tucked away

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.000
in Jill's farmhouse.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:29.100
And that's exactly where Logan wants to play
in his own final game with Halloren to make

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:32.440
it a total of five players, with him being
the sole survivor once again.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:36.400
After planting clues for Eleanor to follow
in the morgue, she thinks she's leading him

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.960
out to the location, with Logan knowing full
well that Halloren will follow.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:44.440
Once Halloren tries to nab them, he's quickly
overtaken by Logan, who advises Eleanor to

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.920
make a break for it and escape.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:50.060
That's when Logan seizes the chance to put
himself and Halloren in one final, terrible

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:50.560
trap.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:54.520
The voice over, which has been dubbed from
old Jigsaw tapes, suggests that it's John

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:58.030
Kramer who's running things and demanding
confessions from the two.

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:01.270
And it looks like Logan fails the test and
is taken out first.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:06.250
But once Halloren confesses to having cost
innocent people their lives, Logan re-awakens,

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:10.630
full-on Jigsaw circa the first Saw-style,
and reveals himself to be the orchestrator

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:11.260
of this trap.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:14.200
And Logan has made a game Halloren cannot
win.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:15.540
An alibi

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.820
Eleanor's part in all of this is interesting
to say the least.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:23.720
At first, she seems to be a perfect distraction
for investigators due to her extracurricular

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:24.220
activities.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:27.200
And then she seems to be a budding love interest
for the widower.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.810
But in the end, Logan says she's just a pawn
meant to provide him an alibi and support

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:33.680
his story that Halloren tried to kill them.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.860
But there may be more to her than meets the
eye.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:40.000
After all, Logan seems to be doing this solely
to punish Halloren, and now that he's brought

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.620
his targets to justice, he has a life to get
back to.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:46.380
But Eleanor seems just weird enough to fill
the shoes of a Jigsaw emulator.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:50.180
She's obviously good at building traps and
has no family to speak of.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:54.240
And even though she doesn't know she's just
worked with Jigsaw's latest protege, she'll

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:58.350
probably find out eventually because Logan
can't possibly explain why Halloren's head

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.360
ends up looking like an octopus in the end.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:01.720
Thanks for watching!

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.820
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.040
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

